THIS FILE IS NOT YET COMPLETE. IT NEEDS THE LICENCE TEXT PASTED IN BELOW.
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The licence chosen for this project is the GNU Affero General Public License,
version 3, and no later version. That choice is deliberate and is explained in
CREDITS.md: Pantry is a web app, so it is *served* rather than *distributed*,
and the ordinary GPL's obligations would never trigger. The AGPL's section 13
is the clause that does — it says that if you run a modified copy as a service
other people use over a network, you have to offer them the source of what you
are running. For an app whose whole value is that it can be honest about where
its numbers come from, that is the right condition to attach.

The full text was deliberately not written from memory. Reproducing a licence
approximately is worse than not shipping one at all, because a licence that
differs from the canonical text in some small way is a licence nobody can rely
on, including you. Fetch the real thing and replace everything above this line
and this notice with it:

    curl -o LICENSE https://www.gnu.org/licenses/agpl-3.0.txt

Then add the copyright line back at the top, and this file is done.

Until that is finished, the position is: the code in this repository is offered
under AGPL-3.0-only as identified by the SPDX line above, and the canonical
terms are those published at https://www.gnu.org/licenses/agpl-3.0.html

The data and the photographs are NOT covered by this licence, and are not the
authors' to relicense. See CREDITS.md, which names each source and its terms.
